1. @Transactional internally kaise work karta hai?
        Answer: Spring AOP proxy ke through method call intercept karta hai. Transaction manager transaction start ya join karta hai.
                Method successful ho to commit aur applicable exception par rollback hota hai.

2. User save ho gaya, lekin payment save karte waqt exception aa gayi. Kya hoga?
        Answer: Agar dono operations same transaction mein hain aur RuntimeException aati hai, to default behavior mein dono
                database changes rollback ho jaayenge.

3. RuntimeException aur checked exception par rollback ka kya difference hai?
        Answer: By default RuntimeException aur Error par rollback hota hai. Checked exceptions, jaise IOException, par default rollback nahi hota.
                `rollbackFor = Exception.class` se rule customize kar sakte hain.

4. Ek @Transactional method same class ke doosre @Transactional method ko call kare to kya hoga?
        Answer: Default proxy-based mode mein self-invocation proxy ko bypass karti hai. Isliye called method ka transactional
                annotation independently apply nahi hota; outer transaction phir bhi active ho sakta hai.

5. Propagation.REQUIRED aur REQUIRES_NEW mein kya difference hai?
        Answer: REQUIRED existing transaction join karta hai, ya naya start karta hai. REQUIRES_NEW existing transaction ko suspend karke
                independent naya transaction start karta hai.

6. @Transactional(readOnly = true) kya karta hai?
        Answer: Ye transaction ko read-only intent ke saath configure karta hai. JPA provider ya database optimizations kar sakte hain,
                lekin har case mein writes ko hard-block karne ki guarantee nahi hai.

7. Isolation levels kya hote hain?
        Answer: Isolation concurrent transactions ke beech visibility aur interference control karta hai. Common levels READ_UNCOMMITTED,
                READ_COMMITTED, REPEATABLE_READ aur SERIALIZABLE hain; support database par depend karta hai.

8. Agar user aur payment alag databases mein save hote hain, kya ek @Transactional dono ko rollback karega?
        Answer: Normal single transaction manager se nahi. Multiple databases ko atomic transaction mein coordinate karne ke liye
                suitable distributed transaction/JTA setup ya Saga jaise design ki zaroorat ho sakti hai.

9. Payment gateway par payment successful hui, lekin database transaction rollback ho gaya. Kya gateway payment bhi rollback hogi?
        Answer: Nahi. External API ka side effect database rollback se undo nahi hota. Iske liye compensation/refund,
                idempotency aur suitable transaction workflow design karna padta hai.

10. @Transactional private method par lagane se kya hoga?
        Answer: Default proxy-based Spring transaction management mein private method ko proxy ke through intercept nahi kiya ja sakta,
                isliye annotation expected transaction behavior apply nahi karega.